    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look to capitalize on several high-upside matchups today, led by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.04) and **Cole Carrigg** (71.23). **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a favorable clash against Andre Pallante; his move to the three-hole provides a significant 6% bump to his baseline, while the platoon advantage against the right-hander further secures his status as our primary offensive engine. Meanwhile, **Cole Carrigg** is the day\u2019s standout speed threat. His matchup against Nick Martinez is bolstered by an excellent 14% park factor and an 18% boost derived from the SP skill profile, making him an elite option to bolster our SB total. **Jacob Wilson** (68.83) also remains a core staple in the utility spot, where his steady presence in the two-hole against Rhett Lowder provides the high floor needed to anchor our counting stats.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the optimizer came at the bench, where **Luis Robert Jr.** (53.71) narrowly missed the final lineup spot. While **Luis Robert Jr.** possesses the power-speed profile we crave, his matchup against Tanner Bibee presents a challenge, and the optimizer prioritized the consistent daily efficiency of **Nasim Nunez** (60.54) and **Heliot Ramos** (59.30) to ensure we don't bleed away game caps on marginal outcomes. We are monitoring the weather closely, particularly for **Gunnar Henderson**, **Denzer Guzman**, and **Drake Baldwin**, all of whom are playing in games with a 33\u201335% rain risk. **Gunnar Henderson** faces the toughest test of the day against the formidable Reid Detmers (xERA 3.44), and while his floor is protected by his elite talent, the combination of potential weather delays and a difficult southpaw assignment makes him a candidate for late-inning substitution if the conditions worsen.",
